From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: bornaradusin <bornaradusin@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Sun, 1 Nov 2026 17:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] PC5: 120 Hz output, and frame generation at the display's
 rate (Wine patches 0946, 0947)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

With PC5's 120 Hz output on (PW_PC5_HIGH_REFRESH=1) and a TV that takes
VideoOut's high-frame-rate mode, RADV opens the display at 119.88 Hz
(PC5's patches/radv 0004; the app's param.json declares it) and the title
tells Wine so (WINE_PS5_REFRESH=120), whose display mode then says 120 Hz
(Wine patch 0946, Mihawk OS 0924) and keeps offering it in the virtual
desktop (0947, Mihawk OS 1188), both by Mihawk, unchanged. The log says
"PW_WINE64 120hz wanted=… output=supported|not-supported|unknown"; off,
or a TV without it, everything stays at 60 Hz.

PC5's frame generation holds a game at half the display's rate, now read
from RADV at the first present (wsi_videoout_refresh_millihertz): 30 -> 60
at 59.94 Hz, 60 -> 120 at 119.88 Hz.
