 | 0943 | `ntdll`: a name opened relative to a directory handle (`RootDirectory`) whose descriptor from the in-process server this module can't use (`fstatat`/`openat` failing with `EBADF`, `STATUS_INVALID_HANDLE`) is looked up from the directory's own name, the server's or its NT name's, as patch 0936 enters such a directory; logged the first time. .NET's `FileSystemEnumerator` opens each subfolder that way, and a game's folder with subfolders couldn't be listed (Heroes of Might and Magic: Olden Era, `StreamingAssets\maps\Story_maps`, still after 0936 and 0938) |
 | 0944 | `ntdll`: a general protection fault with error code 0 from SGDT, SIDT, SLDT, SMSW or STR, which the console refuses in programs (CR4.UMIP), is emulated in 64-bit and 32-bit code: Linux's values for SGDT, SIDT and SMSW, Windows' for SLDT (0) and STR (0x40), written to the instruction's register or memory operand; logged the first time. A game's anti-tamper or CPU check that ran one ended on an access violation reading `0xffffffffffffffff`. The finding is PS5_MihawkOS's (its 2102) |
 | 0945 | `ntdll`: on PS5, a synchronous read of 64 KiB or less from a regular file is served from a 512 KiB piece read at once (four a process, by device and inode, checked with `fstat`; this process's writes and size changes forget them). The console's kernel reads exactly what is asked, so 4 KiB reads came at 88 MB/s. From PS5_MihawkOS (its 2082) |
+| 0946 | `win32u` (Mihawk OS 0924): the PS5 driver's display mode reports the rate in `WINE_PS5_REFRESH` (120 when the title opens the display at 119.88 Hz, PC5's 120 Hz output) instead of always 60, so a game paces itself and shows its rate from it |
+| 0947 | `win32u` (Mihawk OS 1188): in a virtual desktop, the virtual source starts at the display's own rate and keeps the modes it generated, so 120 Hz modes stay offered after a game's 60 Hz mode change |
 | 0953 | `wow64`: a 32-bit caller's allocation with its own address requirements (an alignment) and no highest address is kept below the 32-bit process's limit, as on Windows; it landed above 4 GiB and the game faulted on the address's low half. From PS5_MihawkOS |
 | 0954 | `server`: on PS5, an opened file's directory is resolved with `realpath` once and kept (64 entries, checked by device and inode), so an open costs two system calls instead of one a path component. From PS5_MihawkOS (its 2080) |
 | 0955 | `ntdll`: on PS5, the directories a process resolved are kept by their upper-cased Windows path (1024 slots) and a lookup starts from the longest one, checked with one `fstatat`; a directory's case sensitivity is not asked (the console's disk is). From PS5_MihawkOS (its 2081) |
